From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:03:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: report failed charge limit
 requests

Both charge control setters kept the cached thresholds unchanged when
the firmware request failed, but returned 0, so a write to
charge_control_start_threshold or charge_control_end_threshold looked
successful while nothing was set. Return the request's error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index 2b30436404b5..4546a9e86fc4 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -862,7 +862,7 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_set_charge_start_threshold(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr,
 		battmgr->info.charge_ctrl_end = target_soc;
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qcom_battmgr_set_charge_end_threshold(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr, int end_soc)
@@ -883,7 +883,7 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_set_charge_end_threshold(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr, i
 		battmgr->info.charge_ctrl_end = end_soc;
 	}
 
-	return 0;
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qcom_battmgr_charge_control_thresholds_init(struct qcom_battmgr *battmgr)
-- 
2.43.0

